From f89baf5be042cf2e03fd0caf922b84462fe3a773 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: test <test@example.com>
Date: Wed, 11 Nov 2026 19:29:01 +0000
Subject: [PATCH] perf(loader): retain UMA buddy sponge across post-load weight
 processing

Upstream base: local-inference-lab/vllm 19f2c20ed4d64ae22bd009ceacadd85e2a81e354 (after candidate-54 0799).

Rationale:
In nvidia.ko (nv_alloc_system_pages), non-contiguous system-memory cuMemCreate allocations satisfy 20 MiB segments by draining smaller free physical buddy orders from 64 KiB upward (64K -> 128K -> 256K -> 512K -> 1M) before touching >= 2 MiB contiguous blocks. On GB10 (SM121, 24 MiB physically-indexed L2), scattered 64 KiB..256 KiB physical fragments self-conflict across L2 cache slices during 15-20 MiB decode L2 weight prefetches (+12-13% slower than >= 2 MiB contiguous blocks). Previously, _allocate_order13_sponge returned empty on all 4 KiB-page kernels and on 64 KiB-page kernels whenever 512 MiB (Order-13) blocks reached 0, budgeted free memory from cudaMemGetInfo (MemFree) instead of UMA /proc/meminfo MemAvailable, and released its sponge at the end of create_model() before process_weights_after_loading() re-allocated repacked MoE expert slabs and FP8 block-scale words.

Changes:
- Generalize direct_loader.py buddy sponge across both 4 KiB and 64 KiB base page sizes (parse_buddyinfo_blocks, select_buddy_sponge_target, _available_uma_or_gpu_bytes, _try_thp_buddy_defrag): soak >= 64 KiB sub-2 MiB buddy fragments (or < 512 MiB when Order-13 blocks exist) bounded by both UMA MemAvailable (6 GiB untouched floor) and remaining >= 64 KiB buddy capacity so allocations never fall into order-4 slowpath page-cache reclaim.
- Retain model._direct_buddy_sponge across create_model -> load_weights -> process_weights_after_loading (released in BaseModelLoader.load_model finally via release_weight_arena_sponge) so repacked TileLang MoE slabs, tails, and FP8 scale words also draw >= 2 MiB contiguous blocks; allocate replaceable MoE slabs before the persistent dense weight arena so _direct_weight_arena receives the highest contiguous buddy orders.
- Refresh module slice views (_refresh_views, e.g. shard_weight) after arena rebinding and copy TILE_CONTIGUOUS_FP8 repacked tiles (wq_b / indexer.wq_b) in place into the contiguous arena storage instead of stranding arena slices.
- Bind contiguous weight arenas in DummyModelLoader.create_model on CUDA (when online quantization is not active) and zero non-floating-point CUDA parameters in initialize_single_dummy_weight.

Quality implications:
None. Weight values, dtypes, and kernel arithmetic are bit-identical.

Tests:
- pytest tests/model_executor/model_loader/test_direct_loader.py tests/model_executor/model_loader/test_direct_loader_cuda.py tests/kernels/quantization/test_deepseek_v41_tilelang_linear.py (193 passed on GB10).

Upstream status: spark-ds41f local candidate patch.
